---
flowchart BT
    accTitle: How Vis runs a task and turns repeated work into tools
    accDescr: In each step, the model writes one Python program. The program calls Vis tools and extension functions and prints the results for the next step. Vis saves the sessions and the helpers. You can turn repeated steps into an extension with tests, and the model finds its functions with apropos.
    subgraph each["Each step"]
        direction LR
        step["The model writes<br/>one Python program"] --> tools["Vis tools and<br/>extension functions"]
        tools --> results["Printed results"]
        results -- "next step" --> step
    end
    subgraph across["Across sessions"]
        direction LR
        saved[("Saved sessions<br/>and helpers")] -- "repeated steps" --> ext["Your extension<br/>with tests"]
    end
    each -- "saved" --> across
    across -. "found with apropos" .-> each
